1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,749
Ava: What if adding a new accelerator to a serving framework took less than a week?
Ava：如果给服务框架添加一种新加速器，耗时不到一周，会怎样？

2
00:00:05,749 --> 00:00:15,902
That’s what happened when a two-person team brought SGLang to IBM Spyre with AI coding agents, using a plugin of roughly 1,500 lines.
当一个两人团队借助 AI 编程代理，使用一个约 1,500 行的插件将 SGLang 接入 IBM Spyre 时，事情就这样发生了。

3
00:00:15,902 --> 00:00:28,948
Brian: And the result was measurable: on Spyre, SGLang reached approximately 3.6× the throughput of the reference PyTorch inference implementation using torch-spyre.
Brian：结果是可量化的：在 Spyre 上，SGLang 的吞吐量约为使用 torch-spyre 的参考 PyTorch 推理实现的 3.6×。

4
00:00:28,948 --> 00:00:37,060
On the measured workloads for Granite 3.3 8B and Gemma 4 26B A4B, SGLang was on par with vLLM.
在针对 Granite 3.3 8B 和 Gemma 4 26B A4B 测得的工作负载上，SGLang 与 vLLM 持平。

5
00:00:37,060 --> 00:00:40,115
Ava: Let’s unpack why that moved so quickly.
Ava：我们来拆解一下它为何推进得这么快。

6
00:00:40,115 --> 00:00:48,339
Spyre is IBM’s accelerator for enterprise AI inference, and torch-spyre registers it as a PyTorch device.
Spyre 是 IBM 面向企业 AI 推理的加速器，torch-spyre 会将它注册为 PyTorch 设备。

7
00:00:48,339 --> 00:00:56,130
It also connects Spyre to torch.compile, so the hardware appears through standard PyTorch APIs.
它还把 Spyre 接入 torch.compile，让硬件能够通过标准 PyTorch API 使用。

8
00:00:56,130 --> 00:00:58,933
Brian: That shared layer was the starting point.
Brian：这层共享能力就是起点。

9
00:00:58,933 --> 00:01:09,462
The team could use existing PyTorch implementations of Spyre operations as reference code, then adapt the integration code to SGLang’s backend interfaces.
团队可以把 Spyre 操作的现有 PyTorch 实现作为参考代码，再将集成代码适配到 SGLang 的后端接口。

10
00:01:09,462 --> 00:01:16,376
The AI agents mainly connected hardware support that already existed to a new serving framework.
AI 代理主要是把已有的硬件支持接入新的服务框架。

11
00:01:16,376 --> 00:01:19,702
Ava: What actually changed in SGLang?
Ava：SGLang 实际改了什么？

12
00:01:19,702 --> 00:01:22,833
Brian: Four small patches extended backend support.
Brian：四个小补丁扩展了后端支持。

13
00:01:22,833 --> 00:01:28,454
Two made existing execution paths available without CUDA-specific dependencies.
其中两个让现有执行路径无需 CUDA 专属依赖即可使用。

14
00:01:28,454 --> 00:01:35,997
The other two registered Spyre as a supported device and as an attention backend that does not use Triton.
另外两个将 Spyre 注册为受支持的设备，以及不使用 Triton 的注意力后端。

15
00:01:35,997 --> 00:01:44,388
The compatibility changes can also help other accelerators, while the registration changes are specific to Spyre.
兼容性改动也能帮助其他加速器，而注册改动则仅针对 Spyre。

16
00:01:44,388 --> 00:01:50,186
Ava: So the plugin stayed small because SGLang already separated the integration points?
Ava：所以，SGLang 已经把集成点分开，插件才能保持小巧？

17
00:01:50,186 --> 00:01:50,831
Brian: Exactly.
Brian：没错。

18
00:01:50,831 --> 00:01:59,135
Platform registration, the attention backend, the KV pool, and operator dispatch created bounded tasks.
平台注册、注意力后端、KV 池和算子分发都形成了边界明确的任务。

19
00:01:59,135 --> 00:02:05,181
The existing scheduler, request handling, and serving loop stayed in place.
现有的调度器、请求处理和服务循环保持不变。

20
00:02:05,181 --> 00:02:14,560
The initial plugin was roughly 1,500 lines, compared with about 3,500 lines for the existing vLLM Spyre backend.
最初的插件约 1,500 行，而现有的 vLLM Spyre 后端约 3,500 行。

21
00:02:14,560 --> 00:02:19,398
Ava: That’s a large difference. Was it mostly less hardware code?
Ava：差距很大。主要是少写了硬件代码吗？

22
00:02:19,398 --> 00:02:21,264
Brian: A major part came from reuse.
Brian：很大一部分来自复用。

23
00:02:21,264 --> 00:02:31,111
SGLang’s attention base class supplied the surrounding logic, so the Spyre backend only had to override the inner scaled dot-product attention operation.
SGLang 的注意力基类提供了周边逻辑，因此 Spyre 后端只需重写内部的缩放点积注意力操作。

24
00:02:31,111 --> 00:02:38,540
Reusing that base class accounted for roughly two-thirds of the line-count difference between the two plugins.
对这个基类的复用，约占两个插件行数差异的三分之二。

25
00:02:38,540 --> 00:02:43,258
Ava: What else came from the vLLM implementation?
Ava：还有哪些部分来自 vLLM 实现？

26
00:02:43,258 --> 00:02:50,090
Brian: The team reused how the vLLM Spyre integration grouped inputs into buckets and handled tensor shapes.
Brian：团队复用了 vLLM Spyre 集成中对输入分桶和处理张量形状的方式。

27
00:02:50,090 --> 00:02:54,757
It also reused the PyTorch-based approach to allocating the KV cache.
他们还复用了基于 PyTorch 分配 KV 缓存的方法。

28
00:02:54,757 --> 00:03:07,824
SGLang’s device-agnostic KV pool needed only a single method override for buffer creation, although allocation still needed PyTorch-based handling where the existing path relied on Triton.
SGLang 的设备无关 KV 池只需重写一个创建缓冲区的方法，不过在现有路径依赖 Triton 的地方，分配仍需采用基于 PyTorch 的处理。

29
00:03:07,824 --> 00:03:10,766
Ava: And the ordinary model operators?
Ava：那常规模型算子呢？

30
00:03:10,766 --> 00:03:22,104
Brian: For RMSNorm, SiLU, GeLU, rotary embeddings, and linear layers, the integration connected existing Spyre implementations to SGLang’s operator dispatch.
Brian：对于 RMSNorm、SiLU、GeLU、旋转嵌入和线性层，这个集成把现有的 Spyre 实现接入了 SGLang 的算子分发。

31
00:03:22,104 --> 00:03:28,804
That’s another example of wiring together implementations instead of rewriting them.
这又是一个把实现连接起来而非重写的例子。

32
00:03:28,804 --> 00:03:33,738
Ava: Did every serving feature need a Spyre-specific adaptation?
Ava：每项服务功能都需要针对 Spyre 做适配吗？

33
00:03:33,738 --> 00:03:36,713
Brian: No. RadixCache is the clearest example.
Brian：不需要。RadixCache 就是最清楚的例子。

34
00:03:36,713 --> 00:03:48,460
Prefix sharing is resolved entirely within SGLang’s scheduler before execution reaches the accelerator, so the existing scheduling logic worked unchanged.
前缀共享完全由 SGLang 的调度器在执行抵达加速器前完成处理，因此现有调度逻辑无需改动。

35
00:03:48,460 --> 00:03:53,768
The plugin is available as open source alongside upstream SGLang.
该插件已作为开源项目与上游 SGLang 一同提供。

36
00:03:53,768 --> 00:03:57,622
Ava: For someone trying it, what does the setup look like?
Ava：如果有人想尝试，配置流程是什么样？

37
00:03:57,622 --> 00:04:07,866
Brian: The example assumes the Spyre runtime, torch-spyre, the SGLang plugin, and its compatibility patches are installed and configured.
Brian：示例假设已安装并配置好 Spyre 运行时、torch-spyre、SGLang 插件及其兼容性补丁。

38
00:04:07,866 --> 00:04:21,026
An engine is created with device set to spyre, the spyre_paged attention backend, float16 dtype, page size 64, max running requests set to 1, and CUDA graphs disabled.
创建引擎时，将 device 设为 spyre、注意力后端设为 spyre_paged、数据类型设为 float16、页大小设为 64、最大运行请求数设为 1，并禁用 CUDA graphs。

39
00:04:21,026 --> 00:04:27,444
It then generates up to 64 new tokens for a prompt and shuts the engine down.
然后针对提示词最多生成 64 个新 token，并关闭引擎。

40
00:04:27,444 --> 00:04:30,666
Ava: Let’s be precise about the performance claims.
Ava：我们来准确说明这些性能结论。

41
00:04:30,666 --> 00:04:38,930
The 3.6× figure compares throughput with the reference PyTorch inference implementation using torch-spyre, right?
这个 3.6× 的数字，是将吞吐量与使用 torch-spyre 的参考 PyTorch 推理实现比较得出的，对吗？

42
00:04:38,930 --> 00:04:42,845
Brian: Right. And the vLLM comparison is separate.
Brian：对。vLLM 的比较是另一项。

43
00:04:42,845 --> 00:04:53,862
Across the workloads measured for Granite 3.3 8B and Gemma 4 26B A4B, SGLang’s performance on Spyre was on par with vLLM.
在 Granite 3.3 8B 和 Gemma 4 26B A4B 的测得工作负载中，SGLang 在 Spyre 上的性能与 vLLM 持平。

44
00:04:53,862 --> 00:05:02,680
The relative-performance figure is normalized to vLLM equal to 1.0, with lower values better.
相对性能数值以 vLLM = 1.0 为基准归一化，数值越低越好。

45
00:05:02,680 --> 00:05:05,334
Ava: What’s next for the integration?
Ava：接下来会如何推进这项集成？

46
00:05:05,334 --> 00:05:08,179
Brian: The Spyre software stack is still evolving.
Brian：Spyre 软件栈仍在不断演进。

47
00:05:08,179 --> 00:05:15,919
Over the coming months, the team expects dynamic-shape support, which should reduce much of today’s shape management.
未来几个月，团队预计会支持动态形状，这应能减少当前大量的形状管理工作。

48
00:05:15,919 --> 00:05:25,796
Later this year, they also expect Triton support for Spyre and RadixAttention on top of it, opening the door to additional kernel optimizations.
今年晚些时候，他们还预计为 Spyre 提供 Triton 支持，并在其上实现 RadixAttention，从而为更多内核优化创造条件。

49
00:05:25,796 --> 00:05:30,466
Ava: So the reusable foundation matters beyond this one plugin.
Ava：所以，这套可复用的基础不只服务于这一个插件。

50
00:05:30,466 --> 00:05:30,724
Brian: Yes.
Brian：是的。

51
00:05:30,724 --> 00:05:41,253
Keeping hardware support in PyTorch and integration code at SGLang’s extension points gives future compiler and runtime improvements a path into the serving stack.
将 PyTorch 中的硬件支持和 SGLang 扩展点中的集成代码保留下来，可为未来的编译器和运行时改进进入服务栈铺路。

52
00:05:41,253 --> 00:05:50,064
The next integration can start from concrete implementations and interfaces that both developers and AI coding tools can work with.
下一次集成可以从具体实现和接口入手，让开发者和 AI 编程工具都能据此开展工作。

53
00:05:50,064 --> 00:06:00,118
Ava: Here’s the recap: a two-person team integrated SGLang with Spyre in less than a week using a plugin of roughly 1,500 lines.
Ava：总结一下：一个两人团队在不到一周内，借助约 1,500 行的插件，将 SGLang 与 Spyre 集成起来。

54
00:06:00,118 --> 00:06:08,946
Reuse of PyTorch hardware support, the vLLM Spyre code, and SGLang’s extension points kept the work focused.
复用 PyTorch 的硬件支持、vLLM 的 Spyre 代码以及 SGLang 的扩展点，让工作保持聚焦。

55
00:06:08,946 --> 00:06:29,894
SGLang reached approximately 3.6× the throughput of the reference PyTorch inference implementation using torch-spyre, was on par with vLLM on the measured Granite 3.3 8B and Gemma 4 26B A4B workloads, and used RadixCache without Spyre-specific changes.
SGLang 使用 torch-spyre 时，吞吐量约为参考 PyTorch 推理实现的 3.6×；在实测的 Granite 3.3 8B 和 Gemma 4 26B A4B 工作负载上与 vLLM 持平，并且无需针对 Spyre 做专门修改即可使用 RadixCache。

56
00:06:29,894 --> 00:06:40,355
Brian: That’s the useful pattern: keep accelerator behavior in shared PyTorch code, and make the serving integration satisfy clear framework interfaces.
Brian：这就是有用的模式：将加速器行为保留在共享的 PyTorch 代码中，并让服务集成满足清晰的框架接口。

57
00:06:40,355 --> 00:06:42,220
Thanks for listening.
感谢收听。
